announce	Create GitHub Release	
announce	Create GitHub Release	### First supported public baseline
announce	Create GitHub Release	
announce	Create GitHub Release	- Local macOS Apple Silicon/APFS workflow engine with Workbooks, explicit graphs, frozen briefs/inputs, sealed outputs, legal next actions, human gates, and persistent recovery.
announce	Create GitHub Release	- Current-Attempt resume, terminal-selected results, raw artifact reads, one-time executor replacement, and source-built editable result exports.
announce	Create GitHub Release	- English-default CLI and documentation, explicit Chinese reader/method variants, code-change/spec-dev methods, and source-distributed visual Workbook authoring. English examples use Workbook 1.0.1 and spec-dev uses 0.2.3; installed/running methods retain their frozen versions.
announce	Create GitHub Release	- Standard MIT LICENSE and contributor, security, support, conduct, issue, and PR entry points.
announce	Create GitHub Release	- Store schema 4, cli-result/v4, work-result/v1, and workbook-digest/v2. Only current formats are supported; incompatible data is preserved and rejected without migration or clearing.
announce	Create GitHub Release	- v0.1.0/v0.2.0 are historical development publications scheduled for withdrawal, not supported upgrade sources. Their original qualifications and limits remain in [release records](docs/en/reference/releases/README.md); v0.3.0 does not reuse their evidence as current validation.
announce	Create GitHub Release	- The engine and coordinator skill are planned release assets. sheltie-export remains source-only; the local authoring tool runs from the source tree. Other platforms and physical-device certification are excluded.
announce	Create GitHub Release	
announce	Create GitHub Release	## Install sheltie-cli 0.3.0
announce	Create GitHub Release	
announce	Create GitHub Release	### Install prebuilt binaries via shell script
announce	Create GitHub Release	
announce	Create GitHub Release	```sh
announce	Create GitHub Release	curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -LsSf https://github.com/samuelj1519/sheltie/releases/download/v0.3.0/sheltie-cli-installer.sh | sh
announce	Create GitHub Release	```
